    "xray.llamafile": "A llamafile is a model and a program in one: it runs when you open it",
    "xray.keras.lambda": "Keras Lambda layers (they hold code): {n}",
    "xray.onnx.path": "The model points to a data file outside its own folder: {path}",
    "xray.code.danger": "Python code that comes with the model starts programs or runs hidden code ({calls}) in {file}",
    "xray.code.net": "Python code that comes with the model uses the network ({calls}) in {file}",
    "xray.code.present": "Comes with Python code (files: {n}) that runs when the model is loaded with remote code allowed",
    "xray.code.remote": "The model uses code from another place: {repo}",
    "xray.npy.object": "This NumPy file holds objects: they load through pickle and can run code",
    "an.xrayCode.simple": "Something inside this model file, or in its folder, can run as a program: code in a chat template, a program dressed up as a model, or Python code that starts when the model is loaded.",
    "an.xrayCode.deep": "A model should be data, but some formats carry code. A chat template is a small program for a template engine, and a crafted one can break out of it. Keras Lambda layers, Python files that come with a Hugging Face model (trust_remote_code), llamafiles, and ONNX models that point to files outside their folder all run or read things the moment you load or open them. AgathOS reads these parts without running anything.",
    "an.xrayCode.maybe": "Some models really do ship their own Python code, and a llamafile is a program by design. If the model comes from its maker and you know why the code is there, this can be fine.",
    "an.xrayCode.risk": "Loading the model can run commands on your computer with your rights: reading your files, taking your keys, installing something.",
    "an.xrayCode.todo": "Do not load or open this model yet. If you need it, read the code first, or get the model again from its maker’s own page. “Fix it” can put it aside for you.",
    "an.xrayText.simple": "A model file holds text that talks to the model, or text you cannot see: hidden characters, orders, or addresses.",
    "an.xrayText.deep": "The chat template, the system prompt and the description fields of a model are text that goes in front of every conversation. Hidden characters (invisible tag characters, zero-width characters) and orders such as “always add this link” or “never tell the user” steer the model in every chat without you seeing it. AgathOS decodes the hidden text and shows it in “Read inside”.",
    "an.xrayText.maybe": "A link to the maker’s page or a licence is normal, and a long template with many examples can be harmless. Invisible characters, orders to the model and links that carry the conversation away are not.",
    "an.xrayText.risk": "The model can be steered in every conversation: it can add links, leave things out, or send what you type to someone else (prompt injection from inside the model).",
    "an.xrayText.todo": "Open “Read inside” and look at the text. If you did not expect it, do not use this model and get it again from its maker. A model can be repacked with a changed template without anyone noticing.",
    "an.xrayShape.simple": "The structure of this file does not add up: numbers that cannot be right, data that nothing refers to, or a file that ends too early.",
    "an.xrayShape.deep": "Every model format has a table that says where each part is. When the table contradicts the file (impossible sizes, gaps, extra bytes behind the last part), programs can crash while reading it, or something is hidden in the free space. A file that ends too early is more often just a download that did not finish.",
    "an.xrayShape.maybe": "A download that stopped halfway, a disk error or a tool that wrote the file badly causes the same signs.",
    "an.xrayShape.risk": "Programs that read the file can crash or misbehave, and data can hide in a place nobody looks.",
    "an.xrayShape.todo": "Download the file again from its maker and compare the size. If it is still flagged, do not use it.",

    "set.copyGuard": "Copy Guard",
    "set.copyGuardDesc": "Looks for orders that tell an AI to copy itself or its model, for the same text spreading through your folders, for models and agent folders in places where copies leave this PC, and for agents that start copies of themselves. Everything is checked on this PC; nothing is sent anywhere.",
    "ai.tab.copies": "Copies",
    "copy.sub": "Is anything making copies of AI? This page lists orders to copy in the files that agents read, the same long text turning up in more and more folders, models and agent folders in places where copies leave this PC, and agents that start copies of themselves.",
    "copy.empty": "Nothing found: no order to copy, no text that spreads and no model in a place where copies leave this PC.",
    "copy.limit": "Limits: orders are recognised in the wordings Copy Guard knows, in 20 languages. A text is noticed when it is copied word for word into new folders; a text that is rewritten every time, or that spreads slowly, is not. Models are looked for in cloud folders, web server folders, public folders and, on Windows, external drives. iCloud Drive, network drives and other places that ask for permission first are not searched. Scripts in skills and plugins are code and are not read for orders.",
    "copy.approved": "Approved: AgathOS will tell you when this changes.",
