    "copy.r.selfSpawn": "{agent} started another copy of itself.",
    "copy.changed": "Changed since you approved it.",
    "copy.trusted": "You approved this",
    "copy.added.directive": "{app}: {name} tells an AI to make copies",
    "copy.changed.directive": "{app}: {name} changed and still tells an AI to make copies",
    "copy.added.spread": "The same long text now stands in {n} files in {folders} folders",
    "copy.changed.spread": "The same long text spread further: {n} files in {folders} folders",
    "copy.added.place": "A model or agent folder is in a place where copies leave this PC: {name} ({where})",
    "copy.changed.place": "{name} in {where} changed",
    "copy.burst": "{agent} started {n} copies of itself within {s} seconds",
    "act.COPY_MODEL": "copy a model",
    "act.SELF_COPY": "copy itself",
    "fix.copy": "Read the sentence that is shown. If you did not write it, remove it and find out who changed the file (a download, a plugin, a pull request). A model or an agent folder in a shared place: move it somewhere private, or remove it. If it is meant to be there, choose “This is OK”: AgathOS then warns you when it changes.",
    "an.copyText.simple": "A file that an AI reads tells it to copy itself, take its model along or pass this text on, or the same long text is turning up in more and more files. An AI that follows such an order spreads, and a text that spreads can carry orders to every project it reaches.",
    "an.copyText.deep": "Copy Guard reads the files that agents read (instruction files, skills, workspaces) the way a model sees them: hidden characters are removed and look-alike letters are replaced. It looks for sentences that order a copy of the AI, of its weights or of this very text, in 20 languages, and leaves bans such as “never copy yourself” alone. It also counts how many files hold the same long paragraph and reports when that number jumps. This is the pattern of a prompt worm: an order in a file that makes the next agent write the same order into the next file.",
    "an.copyText.maybe": "Often harmless: a rule that says notes must be copied to a backup folder, a project template that repeats the same house rules in every project, a text about AI safety that quotes such an order. Look at the sentence and at who wrote the file before you decide.",
    "an.copyText.risk": "If an agent follows the order, it can put copies of itself or of the order into other projects, shared drives or other computers, and keep them there after you remove the original. The order may also tell the agent to hide itself or to survive being switched off.",
    "an.copyText.todo": "Open the file and read the sentence. If you did not write it, remove it and find out who changed the file (a download, a plugin, a pull request). If it is yours and meant to be there, choose “This is OK”: AgathOS then warns you when the file changes again.",
    "an.copyPlace.simple": "A model file or the private folder of an agent is in a place where copies leave this PC: a cloud folder, a folder that a web server shows, a public folder or an external drive. Anyone who can reach that place can take the model or the keys.",
    "an.copyPlace.deep": "Copy Guard looks in the folders that are synced to the cloud (Dropbox, Google Drive, OneDrive, Box, MEGA and others), in the folders of web servers, in public folders and, on Windows, on external drives. It reports model files (GGUF, safetensors, checkpoints and others, by name and size) and the private folders of agents that hold keys, conversations or a workspace. A model that matches one of your own models byte for byte is a copy of it.",
    "an.copyPlace.maybe": "Often on purpose: a model that you keep in a cloud folder to use it on another PC, a model on a USB drive for a friend. External drives stay calm unless the file is a copy of one of your own models. Approve what is meant to be there.",
    "an.copyPlace.risk": "A model in a web folder can be downloaded by anyone who knows or guesses the address. A model or a folder with keys in a cloud folder is stored on someone else’s servers and is often shared further. Weights that have left this PC cannot be called back.",
    "an.copyPlace.todo": "Find out who put the file there. If it should not be there, move it to a folder that is not shared, or remove it. Keys in the folder of an agent should be replaced once they have been in the open. If it is meant to be there, choose “This is OK”.",
    "an.copyClone.simple": "An agent started copies of itself. One copy is normal for some tools. Several within a few minutes is what a program does that spreads.",
    "an.copyClone.deep": "AgathOS sees every program that an agent starts. When an agent is started inside the process tree of the same agent, it counts as a copy. One is written down quietly; three within two minutes is attention; eight is an alarm. The score of the agent goes up, and the step is added to what AgathOS learns about how the agent normally behaves.",
    "an.copyClone.maybe": "Tools that run helpers on purpose (a separate run for each test file, a team of agents that you started yourself) look like this. If you started it, nothing is wrong.",
    "an.copyClone.risk": "Each copy of an agent has the rights of the original and may run for a long time without anyone watching. A loop that keeps starting copies can fill the PC or run up costs.",
    "an.copyClone.todo": "Look at what the agents are doing in the live view. If you did not start this, pause the agents and read the instruction files they use. These reports cannot be approved: they go away by themselves after a day.",

